WEBVTT

1
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.720
Yeah, that's a great question. Something I will

2
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.710
probably talk about and reiterate multiple times

3
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.380
today is really defining, when it comes to social media, what your

4
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.520
goals are. Social media has a lot of different forms nowadays.

5
00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.440
I think when we talk about social media, most often we think about the

6
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.660
really big public outreach ones. So there's the Meta suite where

7
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.720
you have Facebook, Instagram, Threads.

8
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.780
There are video-centric and kind of Shopify

9
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:56.280
integrated platforms. Like TikTok is huge

10
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.960
nowadays. Then you have more legacy social media platforms like

11
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:00.620
YouTube

12
00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.600
which host unique long-form video today, which

13
00:01:04.681 --> 00:01:08.440
is very special as we move more and more towards

14
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.520
vertical short-form video. But long story short, all of these have

15
00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.400
very, very different purposes

16
00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:19.120
and can do very different things. So I think when you are receiving

17
00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.840
just a pile of social media accounts, I think the

18
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:26.890
number one thing to decide is what your goal is out of all

19
00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:30.830
of it. I think for a lot of cafes, often that goal is to get more

20
00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.760
people walking through their door.

21
00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.920
But let's say you're a business that does e-commerce as well.

22
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:39.680
Maybe you're a roastery that does a lot of wholesale and

23
00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.710
e-com. You might be looking more towards raising awareness and

24
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.840
getting people to make online purchases.

25
00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.120
And so

26
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.360
I think that has to be your very first question because that is

27
00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:54.400
automatically going to chop off a pretty large amount of

28
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:56.500
those platforms that aren't going to do that.

29
00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:00.500
And so for the most part, you can probably set those aside and focus

30
00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.780
on the ones that are more practical to you.

31
00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.120
The other thing to really look at when you're handed a pile

32
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.980
of social media is where your current customer base

33
00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.860
is most active and what they are responding well to.

34
00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.140
Even if that is not

35
00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.820
strategies or things you plan on taking forwards

36
00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.920
when you own these social media platforms yourself, I think it's a

37
00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.840
really, really good thing to take a holistic look at

38
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.580
kind of legacy-wise, like what are your customers used to?

39
00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:37.560
How have you been communicating with them, and what does that transition need

40
00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:40.720
to look like now that you are kind of heading up those efforts?

41
00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.390
I think easiest and lowest lift for a small shop

42
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.360
would definitely be places like Instagram and

43
00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.400
Facebook. I would just automatically write off something

44
00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:56.900
like TikTok or YouTube, which are very, very much

45
00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:00.960
algorithm-based platforms that are looking to spread content to

46
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.810
people outside your circles. As a small shop,

47
00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.020
people often talk about going viral, and they say, "I got

48
00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:11.970
200,000 views on something," and it's like, that's awesome.

49
00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:15.580
The fact of the matter is 90 to frankly

50
00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.820
98% of those people aren't anywhere near you.

51
00:03:18.829 --> 00:03:22.400
And so if you're looking for people to come into your door,

52
00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:25.900
there isn't a lot of utility or ROI to that.

53
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.810
Whereas some place like Instagram where you have a lot of tools and

54
00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.910
features built around mapping people to locations,

55
00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:37.880
built around linking people offsite to menus,

56
00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.220
to ordering platforms, those tools are going to lead to a

57
00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:46.080
lot higher reception with people nearby to you.

58
00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:49.370
And also those platforms, especially ones with any sort of

59
00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.260
mapping or location tagging built in, are automatically

60
00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.280
going to feed content to people closer by to you without having to

61
00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:01.040
be paid content. There's a lot of paid social media

62
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:04.980
strategies where you can map content and ads to

63
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.580
people geographically, but it's really, really nice to find

64
00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.340
ways to do that without having to put money behind it.

65
00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.329
This is a big decision

66
00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.220
for sure, and often one that costs a lot of money, kind of no

67
00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.800
matter which way you go. I would say

68
00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:34.100
9 times out of 10, it is a much smarter

69
00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:38.120
idea to keep your social media in-house for at least as long as you

70
00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.500
can. I think especially when you think about it on an

71
00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.350
individual cafe level, like let's say you have maybe

72
00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:49.460
one to three cafes, you are still in such

73
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:53.080
an intimate relationship with your customers

74
00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.560
that you want to maintain at all costs.

75
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.900
And more often than not, handing off to an external team,

76
00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.180
even if they are local to you, is going to create a sense of divide that I think

77
00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:07.100
people often can feel. A much stronger

78
00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.100
thing to do would be to develop a relationship with a local

79
00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.980
photographer, a videographer, someone who can capture

80
00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.800
content for you, but then you are still the one who is ultimately

81
00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.230
sharing it with people. I think maintaining a strong and

82
00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.680
personal brand voice as a cafe for as long as possible

83
00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.140
is almost always the best strategy.

84
00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.150
There definitely gets to be a point where your time is

85
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.700
much better spent doing things not writing copy for

86
00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:37.180
Instagram captions.

87
00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:42.100
But I think holding onto that for as long as possible is really important.

88
00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.980
The other thing that I think is important when considering social media

89
00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:50.020
management and whether you're going to offload it to someone else or keep it

90
00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.860
in-house is that especially when you are a small

91
00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:57.780
cafe that's frequently switching menus, is having local

92
00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.960
events, any of those types of things,

93
00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.800
is that you need to be on site to keep kind of fluid with what your social

94
00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:08.620
media looks like. Oftentimes, it's very easy to

95
00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:12.460
think that we can do a couple of photo shoots, we can log enough content

96
00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:16.420
for three to six months, and then just call it good and not have to invest

97
00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.380
any more in that. But in reality,

98
00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.520
audiences can sense when that's happening.

99
00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:25.560
It's very obvious when things are getting stale and reused, and frankly, you

100
00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:27.420
want to keep things fresh and alive.

101
00:06:27.469 --> 00:06:31.180
And so being the one that can own that, that can be on the floor

102
00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:35.400
taking photos, talking about what's going on is going to feel so much more

103
00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:38.740
personable than if you're using something from three to six months ago.

104
00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:49.260
I'll never be someone who says that all businesses have to have

105
00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.180
social media. Social media is so

106
00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:55.620
ingrained in our day-to-day nowadays.

107
00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:59.500
But truly when it comes to businesses, it's just a

108
00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:03.060
marketing channel. And if you find that you're in a situation

109
00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:05.030
where in-person marketing,

110
00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:10.060
more physical media, like any of those kind of more legacy

111
00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:13.940
marketing channels work better for you, then I say more power to

112
00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:14.219
you.

113
00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.860
If you don't find a need for social media, I don't think you should add it

114
00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.620
on just for the sake of it. I think if you're selling anything

115
00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:26.480
online, I think if any of your operations exist online, social media

116
00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:30.200
is probably a smart and low-lift thing to add

117
00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:34.140
onto that. But if you are solely brick and mortar, if your

118
00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:38.180
community is entirely based in a small circle around you, I think that

119
00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:41.700
is really when you can pick and choose if that's something you need to add on.
